# MemNet Lite under Multitask Mode

**WHEN** Multitask Mode is on, or Task / background sub-agents are active:
open and follow **memnet-lite-multitask**. For multi-wave spawn / checkpoint,
also open **memnet-lite-async-checkpoint**.

**ELSE** (single-agent): **memnet-lite-session** / **memnet-lite-local-first**.
In-process MCP is OK.

## Transport (one-liner)

Shared **local** serve under Multitask (`memnet serve` IPC / `MEMNET_IPC_SOCKET`,
or local HTTP bridged to that serve — command **start-local-memnet-serve**).
In-process is OK for solo. MUST NOT use isolated in-process MCP per worker.
MUST NOT use tip MemNet.

## Parent / worker

Parent: one `session_open` / `session_load`; pass `session=` in every worker
prompt; mint/settle `TSK_*` / `USR_*` from `pin_map` not chat; after Bind-ready
spawn one background worker per disjoint atom; end the turn; next turn
`pin_map` first.

Worker: parent's session; `pin_map` first; mutate only the assigned subgraph;
MUST NOT invent parent ids or settle parent `TSK_*` / `USR_*` unless delegated.

Overlapping writes: serialise. Do not assume ACL / RSV is productized.

Chat is never mission SSOT. **tip ≠ face.** Not SysMLEdge.
